 "Department of Microbiology, University of Iowa Carver College of Medicine, Iowa City, IA, 52242, USA."}]}}, {"fullName": "Perlman S", "lastName": "Perlman", "firstName": "Stanley", "initials": "S", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4213-2354"}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1560-1573"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-4213-2354"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "related_data", "wikipedia"]}, "journalInfo": {"volume": "1282", "journalIssueId": 2257823, "dateOfPublication": "2015 ", "monthOfPublication": 0, "yearOfPublication": 2015, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Methods Mol Biol", "title": "Methods in molecular biology (Clifton, N.J.)", "essn": "1940-6029", "issn": "1064-3745", "nlmid": "9214969", "isoabbreviation": "Methods Mol Biol"}, "printPublicationDate": "2015-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2015", "pageInfo": "1-23", "abstractText": "Coronaviruses (CoVs), enveloped positive-sense RNA viruses, are characterized by club-like spikes that project from their surface, an unusually large RNA genome, and a unique replication strategy. Coronaviruses cause a variety of diseases in mammals and birds ranging from enteritis in cows and pigs and upper respiratory disease in chickens to potentially lethal human respiratory infections. Here we provide a brief introduction to coronaviruses discussing their replication and pathogenicity, and current prevention and treatment strategies. We also discuss the outbreaks of the highly pathogenic Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus (SARS-CoV) and the recently identified Middle Eastern Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus (MERS-CoV).", "affiliation": "Department of Microbiology, University of Iowa Carver College of Medicine, Iowa City, IA, 52242, USA.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["chapter-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "NINDS NIH